  "rationales": {
    "U": "证据片段：'every stated requirement must be externally perceivable' – 解释：句子结构基本清晰，但术语'externally perceivable'可能不够具体，影响用户快速理解其含义。",
    "A": "证据片段：'externally perceivable' – 解释：该短语模糊，可能被解释为可观察、可检测或可交互，缺乏明确标准，导致需求歧义。",
    "C": "证据片段：整个需求文本 – 解释：要求需求可外部感知在软件需求工程中是合理的，有助于确保可测试性，但缺乏上下文可能影响其正确性，如是否适用于所有需求类型。",
    "V": "证据片段：'externally perceivable' – 解释：该术语主观，无法直接测试或验证，没有定义具体的验收标准或测试方法，影响可验证性。"
  },
  "suggestions": {
    "U": "保持不变",
    "A": "Every requirement stated in this section must be observable or detectable by users, operators, or external systems without requiring internal system access.",
    "C": "保持不变",
    "V": "Each requirement in this section shall have associated acceptance criteria that can be verified through testing user actions, operator inputs, or system outputs."
  },
  "issues": [
    {"type": "A", "evidence": "externally perceivable", "rewrite": "Every requirement in this section must be testable through direct observation by users, interaction by operators, or interfaces with external systems."},
    {"type": "V", "evidence": "externally perceivable", "rewrite": "Each requirement stated in this section shall be verifiable by defining test cases that involve external entities such as users, operators, or other systems."}
  ]
}

{
  "item": "R1",
  "scores": {"U": 2, "A": 2, "C": 3, "V": 1},
  "confidences": {"U": 0.85, "A": 0.9, "C": 0.75, "V": 0.95},
  "rationales": {"U":"'externally perceivable by users, operators, or other external systems' is vague and context-dependent; 'perceivable' lacks definition (e.g., via UI, log, API response, notification?) and fails to specify *how* or *under what conditions* — impairing shared understanding among stakeholders.","A":"'Externally perceivable' is ambiguous: it conflates observability (e.g., a status code) with subjective perception (e.g., 'users feel informed'), and 'users, operators, or other external systems' introduces scope ambiguity — no criteria for who qualifies as 'operator' or 'external system'.","C":"The requirement is logically sound as a design constraint but lacks alignment with standard requirement quality principles; it does not contradict domain facts, so correctness is moderate.","V":"No test procedure can be derived from 'must be externally perceivable' — no measurable outcome, no pass/fail criterion, no observable artifact or behavior specified; thus fundamentally unverifiable."},
  "suggestions": {"U":"Replace with atomic, behavior-focused language specifying concrete artifacts and actors.","A":"Define 'externally perceivable' operationally via specific, mutually exclusive output channels and responsible recipients.","C":"Keep as a guiding principle but relocate to non-functional constraints appendix; do not encode as a verifiable requirement.","V":"Rewrite to require a specific, observable, and measurable output for each requirement (e.g., 'shall produce an HTTP 200 response with JSON payload containing field X' or 'shall display message Y in the primary UI within 1s of action Z')."},
  "issues": [
    {"type":"U","evidence":"every stated requirement must be externally perceivable by users, operators, or other external systems","rewrite":"Each requirement shall manifest as at least one of the following observable artifacts: (a) a visible UI element or message rendered in the primary user interface; (b) a structured log entry emitted to the central logging system with severity=INFO or higher; (c) an HTTP response status code and body conforming to the documented API contract; or (d) a message published to the designated integration topic with schema-compliant payload."},
    {"type":"A","evidence":"externally perceivable by users, operators, or other external systems","rewrite":"Each requirement shall produce an observable artifact accessible to at least one of the following defined roles: 'end user' (interacting via web or mobile UI), 'system operator' (monitoring via Grafana dashboards or /health endpoint), or 'integrated system' (receiving data via REST API, AMQP message, or SFTP file)."},
    {"type":"V","evidence":"must be externally perceivable","rewrite":"For every requirement, the specification shall define exactly one verifiable output: either (i) a UI state change captured in screenshot + DOM snapshot; (ii) a log line matching regex '^[A-Z]{4,}:.*' emitted within 500ms; (iii) an API response with documented status, headers, and JSON schema validation result; or (iv) a message on topic 'req-out-{id}' validated against Avro schema v2.1."}
  ]
}
